## Summary

**The problem:** `server` didn't compile — tests required a lightweight model list (tags) cache, startup that skips heavy local show hydration, `Capabilities`/`ContextLength`/`EmbeddingLength` in the list API, and the `cmd/launch` inventory carrying tags metadata. Root cause: startup hydration built full show responses for every local model (tensor walks, template rendering) and `/api/tags` rebuilt model details per request.

**Changes:**

1. **`server/model_list_cache.go` (new)** — `modelListCache`/`modelListSummary`: process-local `/api/tags` cache keyed by canonical model name (protocol scheme stripped so keys match). Startup hydration (`Start`/`Wait`) builds only cheap summaries via a `build` seam (manifest + config + GGUF header, no full show response). `List` syncs against current manifests (add new, refresh digest changes, drop deleted/stale, never serves a stale summary), `RefreshModel`/`Delete` serve mutation hooks, `Get`/`Len` for lookups.

2. **`server/model_caches.go`** — added `modelList` to `modelCaches` and started it in `Start`.

3. **`server/model_show_cache.go`** — `runStartup` now only warms cloud entries; local show responses are built on demand in `GetLocal`, so boot cost is independent of the number/size of installed models.

4. **`server/routes.go`** — `ListHandler` serves from the cache (with fallback to the old scan); `CopyHandler`/`DeleteHandler` refresh/delete cache entries; added `refreshModelListCache`/`removeModelListCache` helpers.

5. **`server/create.go`** — create hook refreshes the list cache after a successful `createModel`.

6. **`api/types.go`** — `ListModelResponse.Capabilities`; `ModelDetails.ContextLength`/`EmbeddingLength`.

7. **`cmd/launch`** — `modelInfo`/`ModelItem` carry `Capabilities`, `Size`, `Details`, `ToolCapable`; inventory populated from the tags response; `buildModelListWithRecommendations` preserves installed models' metadata (including alongside recommendation copy).

**Verification:** `go build ./...`, `go vet` (only pre-existing warnings), and the full test suite pass — including `TestModelListCache*`, `TestModelShowCacheStartupSkipsLocalHydration`, `TestList`, `TestRoutes`, and the launch `TestBuildModelList_*` tests. (The one `TestDroidEdit` subtest failure under the harness environment is caused by `OLLAMA_HOST=11435` being set while the test asserts the default `11434`; it passes with the variable unset and is unrelated to this change.)
